 "conclusion": "The ceiling is 31.2% [22.2, 42.1]. Handing the matcher the exact scale and rotation moves it from 25.0% to 31.2% -- overlapping intervals, ~6 pp. At the true pose the true site is the global maximum in only 16/80 pairs, with a median of 22 locations scoring higher. Pose search is therefore NOT the bottleneck, and no ranking rule over band-passed ZNCC can exceed ~31%. The 40-point block requires ~100%, so 40/40 is unreachable ON THIS CORPUS (see scope_correction) on this similarity measure ON THIS CORPUS (see scope_correction). Separately, all three cross-pose consistency rules FAILED badly (sum 2.5%, votes 1.2%, peakiness 18.8% against 25.0% shipped): neighbouring poses are so correlated that accumulating smears the surface rather than reinforcing the true site. That closes the one structurally unused lever.",
 "forecloses": [
